The Ardia Linux host reports the desktop's window-button layout and a window's tiled state to the shell. GTK keeps
the raw gtk-decoration-layout string it parses (Qt forwards to its GTK fallback), a browser window keeps the tiled
edges the compositor last reported and tells the host when they change, and Wayland notifies each change of edges
against the edges it last notified, so a configure the window never applied can't hide the next change.
